  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Closing a hole in the canopy of the Nam Kading NPA, Lao PDR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will conserve globally significant gibbon populations in the Nam Kading NPA by implementing cooperative interventions to protect gibbon populations involving villages, the Department of Forest Inspection (DFI), the Integrated Ecosystem and Wildlife Management Project (IEWMP) and industry. This will be done by: (1) improving enforcement cooperation between agencies and stakeholders by holding a provincial meeting to report on the status of enforcement operations in the NK NPA and surrounding areas, as well as maintaining cooperation between the relevant government agencies and industry partners; (2) strengthening forest-based patrolling and checkpoint operations by supporting substation 1, located in an area attractive to intruders, within the gibbon conservation area, and Pak Beuark checkpoint, located in close proximity to a recently established resettlement village of 700 households; and (3) improving DFI enforcement of the wildlife and aquatic law at key markets known to be hotspots of wildlife trade by supporting DFIs regular checks of markets in Bolikhamxay Province.</narrative>
  </description>
